Almost all of this component's activation sits on the first token of a document (or of a
packed row). There the model has no earlier text to read, so the value depends only on how
that token begins:

- starts with the letter "l" (la, le, el, Low, Love): clearly positive, about +1.4 with no
  leading space and +0.8 with one;
- a word or word piece with no leading space (New, To, We, mm): negative, about -0.5;
  with a leading space (" the", " is"): about -0.3;
- punctuation with no leading space: about -0.25;
- spaces, digits and space-led punctuation: about 0.

Later in a document it is nearly silent. The one consistent exception is the digit "1",
which is slightly positive (+0.04). The component is loud on many other mid-document tokens
too (letter-l fragments, digits, some rare words), but of mixed sign, with no pattern a
short rule can name, so this program predicts 0 there.
